# Optional wireless adb, for headset development.
#
# The Neo 2 never re-enumerates on USB after a reboot, so every reboot costs a
# physical replug. Over TCP that goes away.
#
# persist.adb.tcp.port cannot be used from build.prop: persistent properties are
# restored from /data/property AFTER build.prop is loaded, and adbd pins that key
# to 0 whenever it drops back to USB mode, so the /data copy always wins.
# Triggering on our own property and setting service.adb.tcp.port instead avoids
# the fight entirely.
#
# OFF by default - this opens a root-capable adb socket to anyone on the LAN, so
# it has to be asked for:
#     adb shell su -c 'setprop persist.pn2.adbwifi 1'   (survives reboots)
#     adb shell su -c 'setprop persist.pn2.adbwifi 0'   (back to usb only)

on property:persist.pn2.adbwifi=1
    setprop service.adb.tcp.port 5555
    restart adbd

on property:persist.pn2.adbwifi=0
    setprop service.adb.tcp.port -1
    restart adbd
